<Base title="9. Put it in the water — AquaSense">
  <p class="kicker">Step 9 of 9</p>
  <h1>Put it in the water</h1>
  <p class="lede">Permits before the mooring. This kit has not been in a lake. You are the operator.</p>

  <h2>Permission</h2>
  <p>
    Florida: private water is between you and the landowner. Public water and preserves need the manager.
    Aids to navigation are regulated — see
    <a href="https://www.flrules.org/gateway/ChapterHome.asp?Chapter=68D-23">FWC 68D-23</a>
    and, if the Coast Guard would treat it as a PATON, their PATON rules.
    Hull yellow or white with reflective tape. Do not paint it like a channel marker.
  </p>

  <h2>Mooring</h2>
  <p>Scope for wind and tide. Keep probes off the bottom. Note the GPS fix on first wake so you can find it again.</p>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Pull the EC probe between deployments.</strong> DFR0300-H is lab-grade: DFRobot says it is not for long-term immersion. This kit is a buoy, not a permission to leave that probe in a lake for a season. Rinse with distilled water, recap, store wet-capped as the wiki says.
  </div>

  <h2>What “healthy” last-seen looks like</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A new row about every 15 minutes (900 s) while the battery is up.</li>
    <li>Battery not collapsing overnight if the 10 W panel saw sun the day before.</li>
    <li>DO below 2 mg/L is an ecological hypoxia rule of thumb on the dashboard — not an FDEP lab limit.</li>
    <li>GitHub Pages gauges are fixture data labeled simulated. Trust only the site you host.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout">Do not publish kit readings as regulatory data. Do not claim a named preserve deployment without written permission.</div>
  <div class="checkpoint">
    <strong>Checkpoint.</strong> You have written permission, a mooring plan, and a dashboard last-seen you understand. The project stops being a kit and starts being your station.
  </div>
  <div class="pager">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}build/bucket/`}>← Bucket</a>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/accuracy/`}>Limits and citations →</a>
  </div>
</Base>
